  "why": "Parked accent implementations, kept here on purpose. NEVER remove them: they are the casting work for the accents the Kokoro v1.0 bank cannot produce (true Icelandic, Scottish, Scouse, Nordic, Japanese-flavoured voices). They are NOT shown in the UI because each needs an F5-TTS reference clip (generated from e.g. Piper is_IS / gd / nb_NO voices reading English) plus per-tribe model-id wiring in the speaker resolver; enabling one is a matter of moving its slots up into 'sets' and adding the clip ids to assets/voices-f5. Auditions of the experimental Japanese/Chinese banks live in /tmp/aiva-audition (jf_alpha, zf_xiaoxiao) — they synthesize on the v1.0 model but accent quality is unverified.",
